You can take photographs of real computer components or use suitable images from reliable websites, following your assignment's rules. If you use online images, check their usage permissions and record the source.

How to investigate each component
For each component, try to identify its manufacturer and model, then find its specifications on the manufacturer's website. For example, a CPU's model name and clock speed, or a power supply's rated wattage, are useful details to record.

Tip: If you are investigating the components inside your own computer, you may not be able to see the CPU or cooler clearly without removing parts. Do not dismantle a computer or open a power supply unless you have appropriate supervision.


